## Final Judgement
The fact-check evidence consistently shows that there is no credible support for the claim that the COVID-19 pandemic was pre-planned with Bill Gates' help. Multiple authoritative sources—including the European Commission, CNBC, USA Today, and scientific publications—explicitly state that such claims are conspiracy theories, that no individual or organization is responsible for creating the virus, that Bill Gates had no prior knowledge of SARS-CoV-2, and that pandemic preparedness exercises like Event 201 were not predictive of COVID-19. The scientific consensus points to a natural zoonotic origin, and fact-checking organizations have repeatedly debunked the allegation. No evidence of pre-planning or involvement by Gates exists.

